<title>CHINA: Liu Chong Hing Bank shrs surge on rumour.</title>
<headline>Liu Chong Hing Bank shrs surge on rumour.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Liu Chong Hing Bank Ltd surged on Thursday morning on rumours that a Chinese firm is interested in boosting its stake, brokers said.</p>
<p>Liu Chong Hing shares jumped HK$4.85, or 24.94 percent, to close the morning at HK$24.30. Trading on the shares was suspended from 2.30 pm (0630 gmt) pending an announcement.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a rumour that COSCO may increase its stake in bank,&quot; said Ricky Tam, senior analyst at Delta Asia Securities.</p>
<p>COSCO (Hong Kong) Group Ltd, the parent of COSCO Pacific Ltd, has a five percent stake in the bank. COSCO and Liu Chong Hing officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
